Phase 1c step 2. The skeleton from the previous commit is replaced with
the full recv-thread + bounded-queue + PERF-logged client. Validated
end-to-end against the deployed cuprated server (152.53.133.188:18091):
10 001 blocks from h=1.5M retrieved cleanly, chunks monotonic, stream
closed with ok=1.

Client design (grpc_block_stream_client.cpp):
- open_stream spawns one recv thread that drains reader->Read() into an
  std::deque under mutex+condvar.
- next_chunk_payload pops with timeout. If the queue is full when the
  recv thread tries to push, the thread blocks on cv_not_full -- that
  propagates back through gRPC HTTP/2 flow control to the server, so
  backpressure surfaces naturally instead of buffering chunks in RAM.
  Capacity = 4 chunks on purpose: keeps the memory tight (<~8 MB cached)
  and makes the bp_waits counter reflect real wallet-slower-than-server
  behaviour in the PERF log.
- close() is idempotent: TryCancel on the ClientContext forces an
  in-flight Read to return false, the recv thread exits cleanly,
  destructor-safe even if the caller forgets to close().

PERF logging (Roland's feedback = heavy logging from day 1):
- CONNECT: target + "lazy TCP" note so reader knows OPEN timing is the
  first RPC, not channel creation.
- OPEN:    client_req_id, start, stop, prune, chunk_hint.
- FIRST_CHUNK_LATENCY_MS: explicit one-shot timing from OPEN to first
  Read — dominant during server cold-start, drops after DB warmup.
- CHUNK (per chunk): seq, start, n_blocks, payload_bytes, cum_{chunks,
  blocks, bytes, ms, mbs}, chain_tip, enq_wait_ms, client/server req_ids.
- BACKPRESSURE: separate line when enq_wait_ms > 5 ms — grep-friendly.
- CLOSE: reason (stream_end_ok / client_cancel / stream_error), totals,
  avg_mbs, bp_waits, grpc_code + message.

test_client.cpp + BUILD_GRPC_STREAM_TESTS option:
- Small standalone binary (cuprate_grpc_stream_test) that links the
  library + exercises connect → open_stream → next_chunk_payload loop →
  close. Handy for validating the client against a real server before
  wiring it into wallet2.cpp (next commit). Off by default; enable with
  -DBUILD_GRPC_STREAM_TESTS=ON.

Link fix vs. previous commit: pkg-config link_directories/link_libraries
changed from PRIVATE to PUBLIC on cuprate_grpc_stream so downstream
targets (the test exe and, later, the wallet library) inherit -L paths
for libgrpc++ — otherwise the linker can't resolve it.
